const advantages: GuideCourse = {
  id:'advantages', task:'task2', name:'利弊类', en:'Advantages & Disadvantages', accent:'#d9ff67',
  promise:'不再罗列好处坏处，而是比较影响范围、持续时间与可逆性。', duration:'40 MIN', targetWords:'270–290 WORDS',
  coreRule:'先确认题目只要求 discuss advantages and disadvantages，还是进一步问 advantages outweigh disadvantages。后一种必须从开头就给权重判断。',
  questionSignals:['What are the advantages and disadvantages?','Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?','Is this a positive or negative development?','What are the benefits and drawbacks of this trend?'],
  examFlow:[{time:'00–03',action:'识别任务强度',output:'圈出是否需要 outweigh / positive-negative 判断。'},{time:'03–07',action:'给影响称重',output:'为每项影响标记范围、时长、可逆性和受影响者。'},{time:'07–34',action:'一利一弊深挖',output:'每段选最重要的一项，用机制和例子展开。'},{time:'34–40',action:'核对权重',output:'开头、正文评价和结论是否指向同一判断？'}],
  blueprint:[{part:'P1 · Introduction',words:'40–50',job:'改写趋势；如题目要求，立即回答是否利大于弊。'},{part:'P2 · Advantages',words:'85–95',job:'写最大优势、受益对象、机制与长期价值。'},{part:'P3 · Disadvantages',words:'85–95',job:'写主要代价、风险边界，以及是否可以缓解。'},{part:'P4 · Conclusion',words:'30–40',job:'按范围、持续时间或可逆性做最终称重。'}],
  paragraphs:[
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 01',title:'开头段：先判断题目要“列举”还是要“称重”',purpose:'准确改写趋势，并说明文章范围；需要 outweigh 时必须亮明判断。',words:'40–50 words',formula:'Trend paraphrase ＋ Scope ＋ Weight judgement (if required)',steps:['识别趋势主体、变化和受影响对象。','不用 dramatic / controversial 等题目未提供的评价词。','若有 outweigh，写清总体利大于弊或相反，并预告标准。'],sentenceFrames:['The growing tendency for [trend] has created both opportunities and concerns.','This development offers clear benefits, particularly in relation to …','Although [drawback] is significant, I believe the advantages are greater because …','On balance, this is a positive development, provided that …'],wordBank:['growing tendency 日益增长的趋势','bring about 带来','far-reaching effect 深远影响','on balance 总体而言','outweigh 超过','be contingent on 取决于'],example:'The growing use of artificial intelligence in education offers faster, more personalised support but also creates risks of dependency and inaccurate feedback. On balance, its advantages are greater, provided that teachers retain control over assessment and students learn to verify automated responses.',coachNote:'题目只问 advantages and disadvantages 时不强制判断；但如果问 outweigh，漏掉明确答案会直接影响 Task Response。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 02',title:'主体段一：把优势写成“谁因此得到什么”',purpose:'说明最大收益的受益者、机制、范围与持续时间。',words:'85–95 words',formula:'Benefit → Beneficiary → Mechanism → Wider/long-term result → Example',steps:['选择一个能覆盖较多人或持续较久的优势。','指出直接受益者，避免笼统的 society。','解释便利如何进一步转化为学习、收入、健康等结果。','用具体场景证明，而不是再列第二个优势。'],sentenceFrames:['The most immediate benefit is that …','For [group], this lowers the barrier to …','More importantly, the gain extends beyond … because …','For instance, [scenario], allowing [beneficiary] to …'],wordBank:['lower the barrier to 降低门槛','enhance accessibility 提升可及性','generate spillover benefits 产生外溢收益','in the long run 长期而言','enable 使能够','a broad beneficiary group 广泛受益群体'],example:'The principal advantage of AI tutoring is its accessibility. Students who cannot afford private tuition can receive immediate explanations and practise at their own pace, which reduces the cost of basic academic support. The benefit also extends to teachers because routine questions can be handled outside class, leaving more time for discussion and individual feedback. In under-resourced schools, this combination can widen access without requiring a proportional increase in staffing.',coachNote:'“方便”通常只是第一层结果。继续追问：省下的时间、钱或精力最终创造了什么更重要的价值？'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 03',title:'主体段二：写清弊端的严重程度和可控边界',purpose:'解释主要风险由何产生、谁承担，以及它能否通过制度或行为缓解。',words:'85–95 words',formula:'Drawback → Cause → Harm → Boundary/mitigation → Weight',steps:['区分固有缺点与使用不当造成的问题。','说明损害的概率、范围或不可逆性。','如有可行缓解措施，只用一句说明，不要把文章写成 solution essay。','把弊端和上一段优势直接称重。'],sentenceFrames:['The principal drawback, however, is the risk that …','This problem arises when …','Its impact can be serious for …, since …','Nevertheless, the risk is manageable through … and is therefore less far-reaching than …'],wordBank:['unintended consequence 意外后果','overreliance 过度依赖','erode 削弱','misinformation 错误信息','mitigate 缓解','a reversible cost 可逆代价'],example:'The main drawback is that students may accept plausible but inaccurate answers or outsource the thinking process altogether. This risk is greatest when AI is used without teacher supervision or source checking. However, schools can require students to show working, compare sources and explain how a response was produced. Because these safeguards are practical, the danger is more manageable than the unequal access to support that the technology can help reduce.',coachNote:'提到解决办法的目的，是判断该弊端是否可逆、可控；不要在一段里列出三套政策。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 04',title:'结尾段：明确告诉考官哪一边更重以及为什么',purpose:'用一个称重标准重申最终判断，不增加新利弊。',words:'30–40 words',formula:'Overall judgement ＋ Decisive weighing criteria ＋ Condition',steps:['先给最终判断。','点出决定性标准：覆盖范围、持续时间、严重性或可逆性。','若正文提过关键条件，可用 provided that 收束。'],sentenceFrames:['Overall, the advantages outweigh the disadvantages because …','The benefits are broader in scope and longer in duration than …','This remains a positive development, provided that …','The drawback is real, but both limited and reversible.'],wordBank:['broader in scope 范围更广','longer-lasting 更持久','irreversible 不可逆','manageable 可管理','decisive factor 决定因素','net benefit 净收益'],example:'Overall, AI-supported learning brings a wider and more lasting benefit than its manageable risks. It should therefore be viewed positively, provided that verification and teacher oversight remain central to its use.',coachNote:'“利大于弊，因为利很多”不是称重。必须说清是哪一个维度让它更重要。'},
  ],
  languageZones:[{title:'描述优势',note:'从便利推进到价值。',items:['One immediate benefit is that …','A more far-reaching advantage lies in …','This lowers the barrier to …','The gain extends beyond [A] to [B].']},{title:'描述弊端',note:'写风险来源与承担者。',items:['The principal drawback is the risk that …','This may place a burden on …','An unintended consequence is …','The harm is most acute when …']},{title:'评估程度',note:'为影响加上尺度。',items:['The effect is broad in scope but limited in duration.','This is a serious yet reversible cost.','The benefit accrues mainly to …','The risk can be substantially mitigated by …']},{title:'完成称重',note:'让 outweigh 有证据。',items:['The former consideration carries greater weight.','Its advantages are more substantial because …','The cost is narrower and more manageable.','The net social impact is therefore positive.']}],
  scoreFocus:task2ScoreFocus,
  pitfalls:['把优势和弊端各列三项，却没有一项解释充分。','题目问 outweigh，开头和结尾却不做判断。','同一影响换个说法分别写成优势和弊端。','使用 completely positive 等绝对判断，却忽略明显风险。','主体段变成解决方案清单。','比较时只看数量，不看影响的重要性。'],
  checklist:['我是否识别并回答了 outweigh / positive-negative？','每段是否只深入一个主要影响？','是否明确写了受益者或成本承担者？','是否用范围、持续时间或可逆性完成称重？','例子是否体现影响机制？','比较级和单复数是否准确？'],
  drills:['为四个利弊各标注 scope / duration / reversibility。','把三个浅层优势合并成一条完整因果链。','分别用 broader、longer-lasting、more reversible 写称重句。','用 40 词写一个带条件的正面发展结论。'],
};

const problem: GuideCourse = {
  id:'problem', task:'task2', name:'问题解决类', en:'Problem & Solution', accent:'#ffd36b',
  promise:'找到真正的根因，并让每个方案都有执行者、动作和作用机制。', duration:'40 MIN', targetWords:'275–295 WORDS',
  coreRule:'先分清题目问 causes、problems 还是两者之一。Cause 解释为何发生，problem 说明造成何种伤害；solution 必须精确对应前文，不可万能化。',
  questionSignals:['What problems does this cause, and what solutions can you suggest?','What are the causes of this problem and how can it be solved?','Why is this happening? What measures could be taken?','What problems are associated with this trend?'],
  examFlow:[{time:'00–03',action:'拆任务',output:'圈出 causes / problems / solutions，确认主体段职责。'},{time:'03–07',action:'画匹配箭头',output:'每个根因或问题后面写一个责任主体和针对动作。'},{time:'07–34',action:'写两条链',output:'问题链说明伤害，解决链说明如何切断该机制。'},{time:'34–40',action:'对应检查',output:'每个方案是否处理了正文提到的具体原因或后果？'}],
  blueprint:[{part:'P1 · Introduction',words:'40–50',job:'改写现象，准确说明将分析 causes/problems 与 solutions。'},{part:'P2 · Cause / Problem',words:'90–100',job:'写一至两个相关根因或后果，建立完整作用链。'},{part:'P3 · Solutions',words:'90–100',job:'写执行主体、具体动作、执行方式和预期效果。'},{part:'P4 · Conclusion',words:'30–40',job:'指出最关键干预点与可期待的总体结果。'}],
  paragraphs:[
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 01',title:'开头段：准确复述“症状”，不要抢先塞入所有答案',purpose:'界定现象和任务范围，并概括最核心的问题与解决方向。',words:'40–50 words',formula:'Problem paraphrase ＋ Main diagnosis ＋ Response direction',steps:['把题目现象中性改写，避免擅自扩大到全球或所有人。','确认是原因还是问题，不要混用 cause / consequence。','用一句路线句概括核心诊断与解决方向。'],sentenceFrames:['The growing prevalence of [phenomenon] has become a serious concern.','This trend is driven largely by … and results in …','The main difficulty lies in …','Addressing it will require coordinated action from …'],wordBank:['growing prevalence 日益普遍','underlying driver 深层驱动','consequence 后果','stem from 源于','be associated with 与…相关','coordinated action 协同行动'],example:'The growing volume of household waste places increasing pressure on urban services and the environment. This problem stems largely from disposable consumption and weak sorting systems, and it requires coordinated action by local authorities, retailers and residents.',coachNote:'若题目问 problems，不要把 P2 写成 why it happens；任务词错位会比语言小错更严重。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 02',title:'主体段一：从根因走到可见伤害',purpose:'解释一个核心原因或问题如何逐步造成更严重后果。',words:'90–100 words',formula:'Root cause / problem → Mechanism → Immediate effect → Wider consequence → Example',steps:['选择能解释最多现象的根因，而不是最表面的症状。','用 because / when / as a result 补齐中间机制。','指出具体承担者或环境后果。','若写两个问题，确保它们属于同一条逻辑链。'],sentenceFrames:['The primary cause can be traced to …','When [condition], people / firms tend to …','The immediate consequence is …, which subsequently …','This is particularly evident in …'],wordBank:['underlying incentive 深层激励','single-use packaging 一次性包装','place strain on 对…造成压力','landfill capacity 填埋容量','contaminate 污染','compound the problem 加剧问题'],example:'A major driver is the low apparent cost of disposable packaging. When producers are not responsible for collection, single-use materials remain cheaper than reusable alternatives and consumers have little reason to change. The resulting waste strains municipal collection budgets and fills landfill sites, while contaminated recycling is often rejected. In densely populated cities, this combination raises public costs and increases pollution beyond the neighbourhood in which the waste was created.',coachNote:'好的问题段会让解决方案几乎“自己出现”：如果根因是价格激励，后文就该调整责任与价格，而非只做宣传。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 03',title:'主体段二：方案必须写出“谁、做什么、怎么起作用”',purpose:'提出与前文一一对应、可实施并能解释效果的措施。',words:'90–100 words',formula:'Actor → Specific measure → Implementation → Mechanism → Expected result',steps:['先确定最有能力行动的主体：政府、学校、企业或个人。','使用可操作动词：require、subsidise、restrict、provide。','说明执行方式和遵守机制。','最后明确方案切断了前文哪条因果链。'],sentenceFrames:['A targeted response would be for [actor] to [action].','This could be implemented through …','By making [behaviour] more / less costly, the measure would …','In parallel, [second actor] should …, thereby …'],wordBank:['targeted intervention 针对性干预','extended producer responsibility 生产者延伸责任','deposit-return scheme 押金返还制度','enforcement mechanism 执行机制','incentivise 激励','address the root cause 处理根因'],example:'Local authorities should require producers to finance the recovery of the packaging they place on the market. A deposit-return scheme could charge consumers a small refundable amount and provide convenient collection points in supermarkets. This would give both firms and households a financial reason to reduce contamination and recover materials. In parallel, standardised labels should show exactly how each item is sorted, addressing the confusion that causes recyclable waste to be discarded.',coachNote:'“政府应该提高意识”太空。至少补全渠道、对象和行为变化：通过什么措施，让谁做出什么不同选择？'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 04',title:'结尾段：指出最关键的杠杆点',purpose:'压缩问题诊断与方案，并强调最有效的干预机制。',words:'30–40 words',formula:'Root problem ＋ Most effective response ＋ Expected outcome',steps:['用一个短语概括根因或核心伤害。','点名最有力的主体和行动。','写预期改善，不作“彻底消除”等过度承诺。'],sentenceFrames:['In conclusion, the problem is rooted primarily in …','The most effective response is to …','Together, these measures would reduce … by …','Lasting improvement depends on changing the incentives that …'],wordBank:['lasting improvement 持久改善','depend on 取决于','reduce at source 从源头减少','shared responsibility 共同责任','durable response 持久对策','substantially 大幅度地'],example:'In conclusion, excessive waste is rooted in weak producer responsibility and confusing collection. Financial recovery obligations and clear sorting systems would reduce waste at source and make recycling substantially more effective.',coachNote:'不要承诺 solve the problem completely。现实、有限但可解释的结果更可信。'},
  ],
  languageZones:[{title:'诊断原因',note:'从表面现象深入。',items:['This can be traced primarily to …','An underlying driver is …','The problem is reinforced by …','This creates an incentive for …']},{title:'说明后果',note:'建立影响链。',items:['The immediate consequence is …','This places considerable strain on …','Over time, the problem can undermine …','The effects are felt most acutely by …']},{title:'提出方案',note:'明确执行者与动作。',items:['A targeted response would be for … to …','Authorities could require / subsidise / restrict …','This should be implemented through …','Responsibility should be shared, but not diffused.']},{title:'解释作用',note:'说明方案如何有效。',items:['This would address the root cause by …','By changing the incentive to …','The measure would make it easier for …','This would prevent rather than merely remedy …']}],
  scoreFocus:task2ScoreFocus,
  pitfalls:['把原因、问题和后果混为同一个概念。','方案与前文问题没有对应关系。','每个方案只有 should，没有执行方式。','把所有责任推给个人，却不考虑制度激励。','主体段写成许多短小列表，没有机制解释。','用 raise awareness 代替具体措施。'],
  checklist:['题目究竟问 causes、problems 还是两者？','每个问题是否写清受影响者与后果？','每个方案是否有明确执行主体？','是否说明措施如何切断前文机制？','方案是否现实且不过度承诺？','cause / lead to / result in 的语法是否正确？'],
  drills:['为五个常见问题分别写 actor-action-mechanism。','把 raise awareness 改成三项具体可执行措施。','画两条 Problem → Cause → Solution 匹配链。','用 90 词只展开一个根因，禁止列第二个。'],
};

const twoPart: GuideCourse = {
  id:'two-part', task:'task2', name:'双问题类', en:'Two-part Question', accent:'#cbbcff',
  promise:'把两个问句拆成两项明确任务，并让答案在篇幅和逻辑上精准对齐。', duration:'40 MIN', targetWords:'270–295 WORDS',
  coreRule:'双问题类没有固定内容关系：可能是 why＋positive/negative，也可能是 causes＋effects。唯一稳定原则是 thesis 同时给出两个简短答案，两个主体段一段对应一问。',
  questionSignals:['Why is this the case? Is it a positive or negative development?','What are the reasons for this? What effects does it have?','Why does this happen? What should be done?','What factors cause this, and who should be responsible?'],
  examFlow:[{time:'00–03',action:'给问题编号',output:'在题面标 Q1 / Q2，圈出各自任务动词。'},{time:'03–07',action:'各写一句答案',output:'先写两句最短答案，再为每句补机制和例子。'},{time:'07–34',action:'一段一问',output:'P2 回答 Q1，P3 回答 Q2；复杂一问可稍长。'},{time:'34–40',action:'双向核对',output:'thesis 与结论是否都同时回收两个答案？'}],
  blueprint:[{part:'P1 · Introduction',words:'45–55',job:'改写现象，并用一句或两句分别回答 Q1 与 Q2。'},{part:'P2 · Answer Q1',words:'90–100',job:'针对第一问选择正确论证模式，完成解释与例证。'},{part:'P3 · Answer Q2',words:'90–100',job:'切换到第二问所需逻辑，给出独立且完整答案。'},{part:'P4 · Conclusion',words:'30–40',job:'把两项答案合并成一个总判断。'}],
  paragraphs:[
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 01',title:'开头段：把两个问句都变成可见答案',purpose:'改写共同背景，并为 Q1、Q2 各给一个简洁回应。',words:'45–55 words',formula:'Phenomenon paraphrase ＋ Answer to Q1 ＋ Answer to Q2',steps:['圈出两问的任务词，判断第一问要原因、第二问要评价还是方案。','改写两问共享的现象，不重复整道题。','用不同句法给出两个答案，避免 thesis 只答一半。'],sentenceFrames:['The growing tendency for [phenomenon] can be attributed mainly to …','This occurs for several reasons, the most important of which is …','Overall, I regard this as a positive / negative development because …','Although the trend is driven by …, its wider impact is …'],wordBank:['be attributed to 归因于','multifaceted 多层面的','driving factor 驱动因素','wider impact 更广泛影响','on the whole 总体上','be regarded as 被视为'],example:'More young adults are delaying home ownership, largely because property prices have risen faster than early-career incomes and stable employment arrives later. On the whole, this is a negative development because prolonged housing insecurity restricts both personal planning and economic independence.',coachNote:'好的 thesis 像“两格答案卡”：考官不需要猜哪半句在回答哪一问。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 02',title:'主体段一：严格按照 Q1 的动词选择论证方式',purpose:'完整回答第一问，并用适合该任务的逻辑展开。',words:'90–100 words',formula:'Direct Q1 answer → Explanation → Consequence/example → Q1 link',steps:['若问 why，写原因与形成机制；若问 effects，写影响与承担者。','主题句直接复用 Q1 的逻辑，不要绕场。','解释至少两层，并给具体场景。','段尾用一句回到第一问，不提前回答 Q2。'],sentenceFrames:['The main reason for this shift is that …','A further factor is …, which makes it difficult for … to …','When [condition], individuals are more likely to …','These pressures together explain why …'],wordBank:['housing affordability 住房可负担性','income growth 收入增长','employment security 就业稳定性','postpone 推迟','financial threshold 财务门槛','explain the shift 解释变化'],example:'The principal cause is the widening gap between house prices and early-career earnings. Even diligent savers struggle to build a deposit when rent absorbs a large share of income, while temporary employment makes mortgage approval uncertain. In major cities, young professionals may therefore postpone buying despite having stable occupations and long-term plans. Later entry into secure work compounds this difficulty by shortening the period available for saving.',coachNote:'Q1 段只完成 Q1。提前把 positive/negative 评价塞进来，会让两段边界变模糊。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 03',title:'主体段二：主动切换思维模式回答 Q2',purpose:'针对第二问独立建立评价、影响或解决链。',words:'90–100 words',formula:'Direct Q2 answer → Criterion / mechanism → Impact → Example → Judgement',steps:['重新读 Q2 的任务词，不沿用上一段的原因模式。','若问 positive/negative，选一个评价标准并完成权重判断。','若问 solution，写 actor-action-mechanism。','用明确判断句结束，确保 Q2 得到完整回应。'],sentenceFrames:['This should be regarded as a negative development because …','Its desirability depends largely on …','The most serious consequence is …','A practical response would be for [actor] to …, thereby …'],wordBank:['economic independence 经济独立','housing insecurity 住房不稳定','household formation 组建家庭','intergenerational inequality 代际不平等','net effect 净影响','carry greater weight 更重要'],example:'The wider effect is predominantly negative because insecure housing delays more than a single purchase. Adults who cannot predict their accommodation costs may postpone forming families, moving for work or investing in their communities. Although renting provides useful flexibility, that benefit is less significant when renting is not a choice but the result of exclusion from ownership. The loss of stability therefore carries greater social weight than the convenience of mobility.',coachNote:'Q2 如果是评价题，必须使用明确的评价语言和称重标准，不能只写“它有几个影响”。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 04',title:'结尾段：用一条逻辑线合并两项答案',purpose:'同时重申 Q1 的解释和 Q2 的判断，让全文形成闭环。',words:'30–40 words',formula:'Q1 cause/finding ＋ Q2 judgement/response',steps:['Q1 用原因或核心发现压缩。','Q2 用判断或关键方案收束。','找出二者逻辑关系，用 because / while / therefore 合并。'],sentenceFrames:['In conclusion, this trend occurs mainly because …, and it is negative because …','Overall, [Q1 answer]; therefore, [Q2 answer].','While [main cause], the most appropriate response is …','The phenomenon is driven by …, with consequences that …'],wordBank:['in conclusion 总之','be driven by 由…驱动','therefore 因此','with consequences that 其后果是','overall judgement 总体判断','central explanation 核心解释'],example:'In conclusion, delayed home ownership is driven chiefly by the mismatch between housing costs and secure early-career income, and its overall effect is negative because it prolongs financial and personal uncertainty.',coachNote:'结论不是只复述你更喜欢的那一问。少回收一个答案，会暴露全文任务对齐不完整。'},
  ],
  languageZones:[{title:'回答原因问',note:'从因素走向机制。',items:['Several factors help to explain why …','The most influential of these is …','This makes people more likely to …','The explanation is as much [A] as [B].']},{title:'回答评价问',note:'明确方向和标准。',items:['On the whole, this is a negative development.','Its desirability depends largely on …','The net effect is positive because …','The latter consequence carries greater weight.']},{title:'回答影响问',note:'指明影响对象。',items:['The most immediate effect is …','This has wider implications for …','The burden falls disproportionately on …','Over time, it may translate into …']},{title:'回答方案问',note:'写出完整执行链。',items:['A practical response would be for … to …','This could be implemented through …','The measure would address … by …','Responsibility should lie primarily with …']}],
  scoreFocus:task2ScoreFocus,
  pitfalls:['只回答了更熟悉或更容易的一问。','thesis 写“本文将回答两个问题”，却不给答案。','Q1 和 Q2 在两个主体段中来回跳。','两问篇幅严重失衡。','把 why 误写成 problems，把 effects 误写成 solutions。','结论只回收一问。'],
  checklist:['题面上的两个问句是否都已编号？','thesis 是否包含两个简短答案？','P2 与 P3 是否一一对应 Q1 / Q2？','每段使用的论证模式是否匹配任务词？','两问篇幅是否基本平衡？','结论是否同时回收两项答案？'],
  drills:['随机选题，只用 60 秒写下 Q1 / Q2 两个短答案。','同一现象分别练 why、effects、solutions 三种展开。','把两个答案压缩进一个 35 词结论。','交换主体段顺序，检查逻辑是否仍清楚。'],
};

