  blueprint:[{part:'P1 · Introduction',words:'25–35',job:'改写图题，准确交代对象、地点、时间与单位。'},{part:'P2 · Overview',words:'35–45',job:'写两至三个最显著趋势、排名变化或交叉。'},{part:'P3 · Details 1',words:'50–60',job:'组织第一组相似趋势，给起点、终点与关键拐点。'},{part:'P4 · Details 2',words:'50–60',job:'写第二组/异常线，并完成有意义的跨系列比较。'}],
  paragraphs:[
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 01',title:'开头段：用一到两句准确交代图表边界',purpose:'说明比较对象、指标、时间和单位，不写原因或评价。',words:'25–35 words',formula:'Chart type ＋ What is measured ＋ Where/when ＋ Unit',steps:['读取标题、横轴、纵轴和单位。','选择 shows / compares / illustrates，避免机械替换每个词。','若后段为预测值，在开头用 includes projections 或时间范围交代。'],sentenceFrames:['The line graph compares changes in [measure] among [groups] between [year] and [year].','The graph illustrates how [indicator] changed over a [length]-year period.','Figures are expressed in [unit] and include projections to [year].','The chart provides information on [series] in [place] from [start] to [end].'],wordBank:['compare 比较','illustrate 展示','figure 数值','indicator 指标','be measured in 以…计量','projection 预测'],example:'The line graph compares the proportions of people aged 65 and over in the USA, Sweden and Japan between 1940 and 2040, with the final years representing projections.',coachNote:'Introduction 只需准确，不必炫技。不要写 The graph gives us information，也不要照抄整道题。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 02',title:'Overview：先讲“线的故事”，暂时放下小数字',purpose:'概括主方向、最高最低变化和最明显的交叉或反转。',words:'35–45 words',formula:'General movement ＋ End ranking / contrast ＋ Major turning point',steps:['为每条线标方向：上升、下降、稳定、波动。','寻找共同趋势和异常者。','比较开头与结尾排名是否改变。','选择两到三个特征，通常不写精确数值。'],sentenceFrames:['Overall, all three figures increased, although at markedly different rates.','While X remained the largest for most of the period, Y is expected to overtake it by …','The most striking feature is the sharp reversal in …','By contrast, [series] followed a broadly stable / downward trajectory.'],wordBank:['overall 总体来看','trajectory 走势','overtake 超过','diverge 分化','converge 收敛','the most striking feature 最显著特征'],example:'Overall, the elderly population increased in all three countries. The USA and Sweden rose relatively steadily, whereas Japan remained lowest for most of the period before climbing sharply and becoming the highest by 2040.',coachNote:'读完 Overview，没看图的人也应该知道主故事。如果只写 fluctuate 或有很多变化，信息仍然不够。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 03',title:'细节段一：把走势相近的线写在一起',purpose:'用关键年份和数字证明第一组趋势，并在句内比较。',words:'50–60 words',formula:'Starting comparison → Movement → Turning point → Ending comparison',steps:['按走势相似分组，而不是默认一条线一段。','优先选择起点、终点和一个改变方向的关键点。','用 while / compared with 让数字发生比较。','避免每个年份都写一次。'],sentenceFrames:['X stood at [value] in [year], compared with [value] for Y.','It then rose steadily / gradually to …','After remaining stable at around …, the figure climbed to …','The gap between the two series narrowed from … to …'],wordBank:['stand at 位于','rise steadily 稳步上升','edge up 小幅上升','remain stable 保持稳定','narrow the gap 缩小差距','respectively 分别'],example:'In 1940, the figures for the USA and Sweden were approximately 9% and 7% respectively. Both then increased, although the American proportion dipped slightly around 1980. By 2020, Sweden had moved ahead at about 20%, compared with roughly 18% in the USA.',coachNote:'respectively 只在顺序完全清楚时使用。数字要服务于比较，不能变成逗号串。'},
    {label:'PARAGRAPH 04',title:'细节段二：突出异常线、交叉点和预测变化',purpose:'完成其余系列，并说明它与第一组最有意义的关系。',words:'50–60 words',formula:'Exceptional start → Low/high point → Acceleration/reversal → Final rank',steps:['先说明该线为何与第一组不同。','选择谷值、峰值或加速点。','预测段使用 is expected/projected to。','在结尾完成最终排名或超越比较。'],sentenceFrames:['By contrast, X fell from … to a low of …','Growth was initially modest before accelerating after …','X is projected to surge to … by …','At this point, it will have overtaken both A and B.'],wordBank:['bottom out at 触底于','peak at 达峰值','accelerate 加速','surge 急升','be projected to 预计','a sharp upswing 快速上扬'],example:'Japan followed a contrasting path, falling from about 5% to roughly 3% before recovering slowly. Its proportion is then projected to accelerate after 2030 and reach around 27% in 2040, overtaking both Sweden and the USA.',coachNote:'历史数据用过去时，未来预测用 is projected/expected to。不要把整图都写成 will。'},
  ],
  languageZones:[{title:'上升',note:'根据速度与幅度选词。',items:['rise / increase / climb steadily','edge up slightly','grow substantially','surge / soar to …']},{title:'下降与稳定',note:'不要把所有下降都写 fall dramatically。',items:['decline gradually','dip slightly before recovering','fall back to …','level off / plateau at …']},{title:'变化结构',note:'描述拐点和幅度。',items:['after peaking at …','reach a low of …','a threefold increase','growth accelerated after …']},{title:'跨线比较',note:'强调关系变化。',items:['overtake / surpass …','the gap narrowed / widened','follow contrasting trajectories','remain consistently higher than …']}],
  scoreFocus:task1ScoreFocus,
